{"success":true,"message":"Response generated successfully.","data":{"requestId":"99675760-5673-416a-bf21-cec1e561629a","response":"The `prompt` function in JavaScript works as expected. You can use it to get user input from a web page and it returns the input provided by the user.

Here's an example:

```javascript
const userInput = window.prompt('Please enter your name:');
console.log(userInput);
```

This code will display a prompt box with the message 'Please enter your name:' and wait for the user to enter their name. The entered text is then logged to the console.

If you want to return the same text without displaying any prompts, you can simply use this:

```javascript
const userInput = "Hello, World!";
console.log(userInput);
```

This code logs 'Hello, World!' to the console."},"timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:28:41.887325300Z"}
